25,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
26,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
27,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The data shows a huge disparity in usage, and the cleaning of the fridge has fallen on one person repeatedly. It's quite unfair.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems we've lost our spaces for spontaneous connection, and difficult conversations are happening in public, which is far from ideal.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,May,,"People are spending nearly half an hour just to get hot food, and the desks are becoming eating zones. That's a lot of wasted time.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"We've spent 68,000 yen on outside hires for tiny groups. It's an inefficient drain on our budget that needs to stop.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The walls are far too thin for privacy, and while the room itself is low-maintenance, the noise travels right into the office.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, if we're eating at desks, it explains the mess. But we can't just have a room that's a free-for-all for whoever arrives first.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, if the walls are that thin, a room for loud activity might be problematic, but we still desperately need a private space for dialogue.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, exactly. If we make it a kitchen, who does the cleaning? I don't want us repeating the fridge disaster you mentioned.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, privacy is a luxury, but the cost of outside hire is a fact. We need a solution that saves money and serves a purpose.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Jonathan, you are right. We must balance the need for a sanctuary with the reality that sound carries. Harmony requires thoughtfulness.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"We need a system. Whether it's for eating or meetings, there must be a way to govern the space so it's not a burden.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,A space that allows us to be human—to talk or reflect—would be more valuable than just another utility room.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,May,,"I'm still worried about the ""hidden"" hours. Walking for lunch is a waste, but cleaning a kitchen is a chore.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"The quotes for fit-outs are clear. A meeting setup is more expensive than a kitchen, but the outside hire costs suggest it's a better investment.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Servas,,Let us remember that a room can be a place of rest or a place of work. Both require a different kind of respect.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
