55,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"We have three options: an Open Kitchen, a Quiet Room, or a Meeting Space. Given the usage gaps, a governed space seems best.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"A Quiet Room would provide peace, but a Meeting Space would solve the issue of those awkward, public conversations.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,May,,"An Open Kitchen solves the lunch commute and the desk crumbs, but I dread the upkeep. A Meeting Space is cleaner.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C, the Meeting Space, is the only one that logically offsets the 68,000 yen we're wasting on outside rentals.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Servas,,"A Quiet Room would be a blessing for the nerves, but a Meeting Space, if managed, could bring us together properly.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I agree on the logic. A bookable calendar for Option C would end the ""first-come, first-served"" chaos I found.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, that's a fair point. If it's a Meeting Space, we can finally have those necessary, private discussions without an audience.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, if the Meeting Space is the most professional and requires the least daily cleaning, I'm leaning that way.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,It's the most rational choice. We stop the monthly bleed of outside hire and provide a functional utility for the office.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Servas,,"If we choose the Meeting Space, we must be mindful of the thin walls. We should use it for collaboration, not shouting.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I'm convinced. Option C provides the structure we lack and the utility we need. I vote for the Meeting Space.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,It serves the social void and the professional need. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,May,,It's the safest bet for my time and the cleanest for the office. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,The numbers don't lie. It's the only choice that makes financial sense. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Servas,,"For the sake of our professional harmony and the budget, I agree. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
